28.35 668.98 510.24 -0.57 re f 
BT /F3 10.00 Tf ET
q 0 g BT 31.18 640.46 Td (Part 1. Multiple Choice or True/False) Tj ET Q
BT /F1 10.00 Tf ET
q 0 g BT 31.19 605.03 Td (1.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 605.03 Td (\(1 point\) Which is the correct statement to find the number of employees in each department using table) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 590.86 Td (EMP?) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 576.69 Td (A\) select deptno, count\(empno\) from emp, dept where emp.deptno=dept.deptno group by dname;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 562.51 Td (B\) select deptno, count\(empno\) from emp group by deptno;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 548.34 Td (C\) select deptno, count\(empno\) from emp, dept group by deptno;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 534.17 Td (D\) select deptno, count\(empno\) from emp group by dept;
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 505.82 Td (2.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 505.82 Td (\(1 point\) Find the location that has average salary more than 4000 dollars. Usually each location may) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 491.65 Td (have several departments.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 477.47 Td (A\) select loc from dept, emp where dept.deptno = emp.deptno group by loc having avg\(sal\) > 4000;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 463.30 Td (B\) select loc from emp group by loc having avg\(sal\) > 4000;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 449.13 Td (C\) select loc from dept group by loc having avg\(sal\) > 4000;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 434.95 Td (D\) select loc from dept where deptno in \(select deptno from emp group by loc having avg\(sal\) > 4000\);) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 420.78 Td (E\) select loc from dept where deptno in \(select deptno from emp group by deptno having avg\(sal\) > 4000\);
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 392.43 Td (3.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 392.43 Td (\(1 point\) Find the range of salaries \(min, max\) of each department in the following table:) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 364.09 Td (EMP\(EID, ENAME, SAL, DEPT\)) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 349.91 Td (A\) select min\(sal\), max\(sal\) from emp group by deptno;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 335.74 Td (B\) select min\(sal\), max\(sal\) from emp group by dept;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 321.57 Td (C\) select min\(sal\) as min,  max\(sal\) as max from employees group by dept) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 307.39 Td (D\) select range\(sal\) from emp group by dept;
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 279.05 Td (4.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 279.05 Td (\(1 point\) Find those departments whose minimum salary is more than 2000) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 264.87 Td (A\) select dname, min\(sal\) from dept, emp group by deptno having min\(sal\) > 2000;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 250.70 Td (B\) select dname, min\(sal\) from emp group by deptno having min\(sal\) > 2000;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 236.53 Td (C\) select deptno from emp group by deptno where min\(sal\) < 2000;) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 222.35 Td (D\) select deptno, min\(sal\) from emp group by deptno having min\(sal\) > 2000;
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 194.01 Td (5.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 194.01 Td (\(1 point\) Find the total number of employees hired in January of all years) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 179.83 Td (A\) select count\(*\) from emp where to_char\(hiredate, 'Month'\) = 'January';) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 165.66 Td (B\) select count\(*\) from emp group by deptno having to_char\(hiredate, 'Month'\) = 'January';) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 151.49 Td (C\) select count\(*\) from emp group by month having to_char\(hiredate, 'Month'\) = 'January';) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 137.32 Td (D\) select sum\(empno\) from emp where to_char\(hiredate, 'Month'\) = 'January';
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 108.97 Td (6.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 108.97 Td (\(1 point\) The SQL keyword BETWEEN is used:) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 94.80 Td (A\) for ranges.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 80.62 Td (B\) to limit the columns displayed.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 66.45 Td (C\) as a wildcard.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 52.28 Td (D\) None of the above is correct.
) Tj ET Q
BT /F4 8.00 Tf ET
q 0 g BT 276.73 25.95 Td (Page 1/2) Tj ET Q

